/** @page logger_binreleasehistory logger_bin Module Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    This module is always delivered with %Qore and therefore mirrors the %Qore version.

    @section logger_bin_3_0 logger_bin Module Version 3.0

    @ref Qore::Logger::LoggerAppenderFile "LoggerAppenderFile" raises \c FILE-OPEN2-ERROR when it opens a file name
    with a NUL character instead of opening the file named by the name cut at the NUL character, and raises only
    \c APPENDER-OPEN-ERROR when the file name is not a string.

    Logger interface deserialization restores its native callback adapter. Logger wrappers and
    schema objects inheriting the interface can be serialized repeatedly after restoration.

    A @ref Qore::Logger::Logger "Logger" references its appenders where the garbage collector can follow the
    references, so a cycle through an appender that references its logger is collected instead of being leaked with
    the classes of its objects.  An event created by a logger references the logger:
    @ref Qore::Logger::LoggerEvent::getLogger() "LoggerEvent::getLogger()" read freed memory for an event kept after
    its logger was destroyed.
